+``--sub-picture-text-callback=<pointer>``, ``--sub-picture-text-context=<pointer>``
+    (libmpv only) A function of the application's, and its context, that
+    reads Blu-ray (PGS) and DVD subtitle pictures as text, passed as integers
+    (as ``--wid`` passes a window). Each picture decoded is handed to it once,
+    with its start time and a hash of its pixels; the text it gives (at once,
+    or later with the ``sub-picture-text`` command) is drawn as a text
+    subtitle, with every option a text subtitle file takes. A picture without
+    text is drawn as the picture, and one drawn as a picture stays one until
+    it ends. The function's signature is ``sub_picture_text_fn`` in
+    ``sub/sd_lavc.c``. Default: 0 (pictures stay pictures).
+
 ``--sub-fps=<rate>``
